1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,560
In 1895, H. G. Wells called it an invention.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,138
The Time Machine. The name stuck.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,250
But was the idea new?

4
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,440
Eight years earlier, in Barcelona,

5
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:21,160
Enrique Gaspar launched the anacronópete:

6
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,563
a ship that flies against time.

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,137
It rose over the city like a hot air balloon.

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,870
Six years before that, a New York paper

9
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:38,554
printed a story with no name on it.

10
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,808
A clock whose hands ran backward.

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,001
Its author, Edward Page Mitchell, went uncredited for decades.

12
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,960
So, who built the first time machine?

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,030
A clock, in 1881.

14
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:56,060
A ship, in 1887.

15
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,631
And in 1895, the name.
